  "style": {
    "id": "cubism",
    "name": "Cubism",
    "description": "Analytic-to-synthetic Cubism made from a real 3D still life: a guitar, bottle, wine glass, fruit bowl and folded newspaper on a round café table are rendered from six cameras into render targets, and the flat picture plane fractures into angular convex facets that EACH show the same still life from a different viewpoint (front three-quarter, bird's-eye table top, left, right, eye level, tilted) - simultaneous viewpoints. Facets crack in with dark contour lines, their cameras swing apart, they slide, rotate and overlap; the palette drains to analytic ochre/umber/grey bands with facet passage shading and ink edges, then pieces flip over like card to synthetic collage (flat coloured paper, faux-bois wood grain, newsprint with stencilled letters, wallpaper, charcoal drawing) and the whole settles into a bold flat composition. Canvas weave and brush grain over everything. Every facet pose, crack, swing and flip comes from one seeded plan (facets.js) that also writes the sound.",
